Bug #1: “It looked successful, but half the downstream calls were failing silently”
==================================================================================
What happened
You used exactly this pattern:
    >>>>>>>>>>
    .supplyAsync(() -> callDownstream(), es)
    .thenAccept(...)
    .exceptionally(ex -> { log; return null; }) <= swallows the failure.
    CompletableFuture.allOf(futures).join(); // returns normally
    <<<<<<<<<<<<<
The job “completed”, dashboards showed success, but some downstream systems never got updates.
Fix
Don’t swallow — collect failures and fail the overall request (or route to retry/DLQ).
Or convert to a Result<T> wrapper.
Example pattern:
record ApiOutcome(int id, boolean ok, Throwable error) {}

CompletableFuture<ApiOutcome> f =
  CompletableFuture.supplyAsync(() -> callApi(id), es)
    .thenApply(resp -> new ApiOutcome(id, true, null))
    .exceptionally(ex -> new ApiOutcome(id, false, unwrap(ex)));

Then after allOf, inspect outcomes and decide:
    fail request
    retry failed ids
    send to DLQ
    partial success response

